    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered list of what happens on `POST /api/owners`, as the code actually stands (pipeline defined in `owners.POST.yml`, one step per function class).\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. Without that role the request never enters the pipeline (\u2192 `AuthorizationDeniedException` handler).\n\n## Pipeline steps, in order\n\n1. **`RequireOwnerFields`** *(validation)* \u2014 reads the `@RequestBody` once, requires `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` to be non-null and non-blank. Any missing \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400, names each field). Republishes the body as a variable for later steps.\n\n2. **`NormalizeOwnerTelephone`** *(side-effect + validation)* \u2014 strips non-digits; if no leading `+`, drops a single leading `0` and prepends `61` (assumes `+61`). Requires 8\u201315 digits, and per-country national length (`+61`\u21929 national digits, `+1`\u219210) \u2192 else `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400). Rewrites `telephone` to `\"+\" + digits` (E.164).\n\n3. **`NormalizeOwnerEmail`** *(side-effect + validation)* \u2014 if email present, must match a basic syntax regex \u2192 else 400 (`MissingOwnerFieldsException` on `email`); stores it **lower-cased**. Absent/blank email is left untouched.\n\n4. **`RejectDisposableEmailDomain`** *(validation)* \u2014 if email present, rejects domains on the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException` (400).\n\n5. **`NormalizeOwnerAddress`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 trims, collapses whitespace, upper-cases, and expands street abbreviations (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). Rewrites `address`.\n\n6. **`RejectDuplicateOwnerIdentity`** *(validation, repo read)* \u2014 builds an `IdentityKey` (normalized telephone + email); if any existing owner has the same key \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException` (409). Scans `findAll()`.\n\n7. **`RejectCrowdedCity`** *(validation, repo read)* \u2014 if \u226550 existing owners share the city (case-insensitive) \u2192 `CrowdedCityException` (409).\n\n8. **`RejectDailyLimit`** *(validation, repo read)* \u2014 if \u2265100 owners already have today's business-day `registrationDate` \u2192 `DailyLimitException` (429).\n\n9. **`RejectInvalidPostcode`** *(validation)* \u2014 postcode optional; if present must be 4 digits and, for a known region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099 via city\u2192`Locality`), fall in range \u2192 else `InvalidPostcodeException` (400). Unknown region accepts any 4-digit value.\n\n10. **`RejectFutureRegistrationDate`** *(validation)* \u2014 if supplied `registrationDate` is after `LocalDate.now()` \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400).\n\n11. **`BuildOwner`** *(bean validation + side-effect; transactional from here on)* \u2014 `@Valid @Val OwnerFieldsDto` triggers the DTO's **JSR-380 constraints now** (e.g. firstName/lastName pattern+size, address/city size, telephone `^[0-9]*$`+size\u226420, email size\u2264255, postcode `^[0-9]{4}$`). Maps DTO \u2192 `Owner`; sets `registrationDate` to the supplied date (or today), rolled forward to the next weekday via `BusinessDay.onOrAfter`.\n\n12. **`AssignCustomerCode`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `customerCode = <REGION>-<HASH8>`: region from postcode/city, plus first 8 upper-hex chars of SHA-256 of `telephone + lastName`. No repo lookup.\n\n13. **`CountNamesakes`** *(side-effect, repo read)* \u2014 counts pre-existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive, trimmed), stores as `namesakeCount`.\n\n14. **`DetectPossibleDuplicate`** *(side-effect, repo read)* \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicate=false`; unless `sharesHousehold` is true, if an existing owner shares `HouseholdId` (last name + postcode) but has a different telephone, sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf = existing.id` (first match).\n\n15. **`SaveOwner`** *(side-effect, write)* \u2014 `ownerRepository.save(owner)` and an AUDIT log line (`id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`).\n\n16. **`RespondWithOwnerCreated`** *(side-effect / response, repo read)* \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto`, sets `bulkSignupWarning` (`true` if >80 owners already registered today via `BulkSignup`), responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n## Two ordering facts worth flagging\n- **Bean validation runs late** \u2014 the DTO's `@Valid` constraints fire only at step 11 (`BuildOwner`), *after* the custom checks and *after* the normalizers have rewritten the fields. So bean validation sees the mutated values, not the raw body. Notably the telephone constraint is `@Pattern(regexp = \"^[0-9]*$\")`, but step 2 has already rewritten telephone to a value **starting with `+`** \u2014 so any owner reaching step 11 fails bean validation on telephone. That is what the current code does, not necessarily what was intended.\n- **Transaction scope** \u2014 `govern: [ transaction ]` starts at step 11 and covers steps 11\u201316, committing once at the end; steps 1\u201310 run outside it (their repo reads are non-transactional)."
